ver fallback descendants raw. Good.\n\nWe can compute recursively returning tuple (total_subtree_raw, total_candidate_raw). Then for candidate node, we compute own_stab and store. Also need to know list of candidate children to compare.\n\nWe'll do a DFS from each root. Use recursion; depth may be large but fine.\n\nPseudo:\n\ndef dfs(node_id):\n    total_sub = raw_stab[node_id]\n    total_cand = raw_stab[node_id] if node_id in candidates else 0\n    child_candidate_stabs = []\n    for child in children.get(node_id, []):\n        sub, cand, child_own_stab = dfs(child) # child_own_stab only if child is candidate else None\n        total_sub += sub\n        total_cand += cand\n        if child_own_stab is not None:\n            child_candidate_stabs.append(child_own_stab)\n    own_stab = None\n    if node_id in candidates:\n        own_stab = raw_stab[node_id] + (total_sub - total_cand) # fallback descendants sum\n        # store own_stab for this node\n        node_own_stab[node_id] = own_stab\n    # Now after computing own_stab for this node and having child_candidate_stabs, we can do selection? But selection requires bottom-up decision; we need to decide after we know children's selection status. We'll do selection in a second pass after computing all own_stabs.\n    return (total_sub, total_cand, own_stab)\n\nFirst pass compute own_stabs for all candidate nodes.\n\nSecond pass: for each root, do post-order to decide selection.\n\nWe'll maintain a set selected_ids. Initialize with none. Traverse in postorder (children first). For each candidate node:\n\n- sum_child_own = sum(node_own_stab[child] for child in children.get(node_id, []) if child in candidates)\n- if sum_child_own > node_own_stab[node_id]:\n    # select children; but we need to mark selections later; we can set a flag for this node to indicate it's not selected, and then in children, they will be selected unless overridden. But careful: if we select children, that means we deselect this node and any of